  "family": "learning",
  "category": "basic math",
  "premise": "Three islanders want an equal pile of stones, but their piles contain two, four, and nine. A transfer machine redistributes the fifteen stones into three piles of five and balances their platform.",
  "hook": "What number can stand in for all three piles?",
  "visible_action": "Single stones move between labeled piles; a running total stays fixed while a seesaw levels.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "The arithmetic mean is the total divided by the number of values.",
  "gate": "Show that the mean need not match an original value; avoid calling it universally representative.",
